  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercis_typ\": \"CEFR English Placement Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 5,\n  \"section_title\": \"Reading Comprehension\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2-C1\",\n  \"reading_text\": \"\\\\\nIn recent years, the concept of sustainable development has gained significant traction in various fields. It is a framework that seeks to meet human needs without compromising the ability of future generations to meet their own. This approach emphasizes balancing economic, social, and environmental considerations. \\\\\nThe importance of sustainable development can be seen in its integration into international agreements such as the United Nations' Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs). These goals aim to address global challenges like poverty, inequality, climate change, and environmental degradation. \\\\\nHowever, implementing sustainable development strategies is not without its difficulties. Political will, financial resources, and public awareness are critical factors that must be addressed to achieve long-term progress. \\\\\nDespite the challenges, there is growing evidence of successful initiatives around the world. For instance, some cities have implemented green infrastructure projects that improve air quality and reduce waste, while others are adopting renewable energy sources to decrease carbon emissions. \\\\\nThe author of this piece argues that sustainable development is not just an environmental concern but a fundamental shift in how we think about our relationship with the planet and future generations.\"\n},\n\"questions\": [\n  {\n    \"question_number\": 36,\n    \"question\": \"What is the main focus of sustainable development?\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Emphasizing economic growth\",\n      \"Balancing environmental concerns with social and economic needs\",\n      \"Focusing solely on reducing carbon footprint\",\n      \"Implementing green infrastructure projects only\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Balancing environmental concerns with social and economic needs\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"question_number\": 37,\n    \"question\": \"Which of the following is NOT one of the key aspects of sustainable development?\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Environmental considerations\",\n      \"Social justice\",\n      \"Policy implementation\",\n      \"Technological innovation\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Policy implementation\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"question_number\": 38,\n    \"question\": \"The author highlights that sustainable development is important because it addresses which of the following challenges?\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"Poverty and inequality\",\n      \"Climate change only\",\n      \"Environmental degradation alone\",\n      \"Infrastructure development\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"Poverty and inequality\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"question_number\": 39,\n    \"question\": \"What is the author's stance on sustainable development?\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"It is a necessary evolution in how we think about our planet\",\n      \"It is an environmental concern only\",\n      \"It is not important for addressing global challenges\",\n      \"It is a politically motivated agenda\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"It is a necessary evolution in how we think about our planet\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"question_number\": 40,\n    \"question\": \"Which of the following statements best describes sustainable development initiatives?\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"They focus solely on reducing carbon emissions\",\n      \"They include a variety of strategies to address environmental, social, and economic needs\",\n      \"They prioritize technological solutions over policy implementation\",\n      \"They are limited to green infrastructure projects only\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"They include a variety of strategies to address environmental, social, and economic needs\"\n  }\n]\n}",
